Resetting Bale / Telegram conversations
======================================

Usage (from E:\KomatsoAI):

  RESET_ALL_USERS.bat            Bale only (default)
  RESET_ALL_USERS.bat telegram   Telegram only
  RESET_ALL_USERS.bat both       Both platforms

Read-only preview, without stopping the gateway:

  .venv\Scripts\python.exe tools\reset_user_sessions.py
  .venv\Scripts\python.exe tools\reset_user_sessions.py --platform both

The launcher previews route counts, asks before applying, stops the gateway,
applies the reset and starts it again. Run between active conversations. Users
get a fresh conversation on their next message; they do not have to send /new.
No announcement or other message is sent by this tool.

Use this when publishing changes that require fresh session context. It is
not an automatic update/deployment system. Restarting the gateway alone keeps
the persisted session and may keep the old conversation/system prompt.
Resetting also clears conversation metadata and session model overrides.
Previous messages remain archived, but are not included in the new conversation.
Global configuration and persistent memories are not reset. Code/config/plugin
changes must still be made correctly and loaded by the restarted gateway.

Storage and implementation
--------------------------
Both platforms use HERMES_HOME\state.db for session metadata/messages and its
gateway_routing table for current routing. sessions\sessions.json is a legacy
mirror; database routes take precedence. Counts are conversation routes, not
necessarily unique people. Registrations (including data\telegram_users.db),
fleet databases and transcripts are not deleted or edited by this tool.

The old BAT selected only telegram. The replacement explicitly registers Bale
metadata before parsing native sessions, without loading its adapter or hooks.
It holds the native gateway runtime lock while applying the reset. Each apply:

1. Checks SQLite integrity and rejects pending delegation/delivery work.
2. Creates a unique SQLite backup (including committed WAL data) and JSON copy
   under HERMES_HOME\backups\session-reset\<timestamp>.
3. Runs the installed SessionStore.reset_session on an isolated backup copy.
   Selected routes are seeded explicitly so already-ended sessions also reset
   instead of being dropped by normal startup recovery/pruning.
4. Checks new IDs, empty context, origin preservation and schema compatibility.
5. Publishes only selected session metadata/routes in one SQLite transaction.
   It never replaces the live database or changes unrelated session rows.
6. Updates the JSON mirror and writes report.json with old/new session IDs.

This provides the fresh-conversation effect of /new with the gateway stopped.
It does not replay /new's notification, lifecycle hooks or cleanup of running
agents. Pending durable work causes refusal; finish it before a maintenance
reset. The gateway stop clears its process-local agent caches.

Failures and recovery
---------------------
The launcher does not restart after an apply failure, to allow inspection.
If gateway startup alone fails, do not reset again; retry gateway start.

Inspect the printed backup directory and report.json. A SQLite publication
error rolls back the entire selected batch. A JSON/report write error AFTER
the commit cannot undo the committed reset. Database routes remain authoritative.
The report has planned old/new IDs before commit so a crash can be checked by
comparing those IDs with gateway_routing. Do not blindly rerun after a failure.
Statuses: prepared; validated_before_commit; database_committed; complete.

Keep backups local: they contain chat history. Do not restore the whole DB
over newer activity or copy only state.db while a live WAL exists. Recovery
must be done offline, with the gateway stopped, after checking committed IDs.

Manual gateway start:
  C:\Users\win-10\AppData\Local\hermes\hermes-agent\venv\Scripts\hermes.exe gateway start

Tests (synthetic databases only):
  .venv\Scripts\python.exe test\test_reset_user_sessions.py

Tests cover Bale/Telegram isolation, archived messages, fresh next-message
routing in a new native process, backup contents, stale JSON precedence,
running-gateway refusal, transactional rollback and post-commit mirror failure.
The native Hermes API/schema is version-sensitive; rerun tests after upgrading.

Optional rehearsal using a temporary copy of the current database:
  .venv\Scripts\python.exe test\rehearse_session_reset.py
The source is opened read-only. This does not stop/restart the real gateway.
